  </data>
  <data name="Help_StackLayoutTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Stack Layout</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Help_StackLayoutText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Stacks the two hand halves vertically instead of side by side. Useful on narrow or portrait displays. You can choose which hand appears on top in Settings.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Help_AlwaysOnTopTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Always on Top</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Help_AlwaysOnTopText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Pins the window above all other windows. Great for using as a floating reference while typing.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Help_SettingsTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Settings</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Help_SettingsText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Customize layer colors, names, global hotkey, background transparency, hold threshold, and custom key labels.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Help_RefreshTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Refresh</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Help_RefreshText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Re-reads the keymap from the device. Use after flashing new firmware or changing your layout in Vial.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Help_LayerTabs" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Layer Tabs</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Help_LayerTabsText" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Click a tab to view that layer's key assignments. Each layer has a unique color. Layers where every key is empty (KC_NO) are hidden automatically.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Help_ImportantTitle" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Important: Auto-Layer Switch &amp; Svalboard Input</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Help_ImportantText1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>When auto-layer-switch is enabled (the default), the displayed layer follows whichever layer key you are physically holding down.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Help_ImportantText2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Since your Svalboard IS your mouse, clicking a layer tab counts as a keypress. The moment you click, no layer key is held, so the app switches back to the base layer. This is expected behavior!</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Help_ImportantText3" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>To browse layers manually, turn off auto-layer-switch first (the checkmark button in the toolbar).</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Help_ImportantText4" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>If toggle (TG) layer tracking gets out of sync with your actual keyboard state, use the Reset button to return to the base layer.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Help_Tips" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Tips</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Help_Tip1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>&#x2022; Pin the window (always-on-top) to use as a floating reference while typing</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Help_Tip2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>&#x2022; Right-click any key to assign a custom label</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Help_Tip3" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>&#x2022; Use the global hotkey (default: F12) to quickly show or hide the window</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Help_Tip4" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>&#x2022; Adjust background transparency in Settings to use the app as a translucent overlay</value>
  </data>
  <data name="Help_Tip5" xml:space="preserve">
